 "title": "Volunteer | Ramsey County, Minnesota",
 "text": "Volunteer | Ramsey County, Minnesota Skip to main content Language\nHome Jobs News & Updates Calendar Contact Us\nResidents Residents Overview\nAssistance & Support\nElections & Voting\nEmergency Response & Preparedness\nEnvironment\nHealth & Medical\nLibraries\nLicenses, Permits & Records\nParks & Recreation\nProperty & Home\nPublic Safety & Law\nRecycling & Waste\nRoads & Transportation\nEvent Spaces\nBusinesses Businesses Overview\nDoing Business with Ramsey County\nWorkforce & Business Development\nLicenses, Permits & Inspections\nProperty & Development\nRecycling & Waste\nTransit Sales & Use Tax\nYour Government Your Government Overview\nLeadership\nAbout Ramsey County\nContacts & Locations\nDepartments\nProjects & Initiatives\nOrdinances & Regulations\nVolunteer\nOpen Government\nVolunteer\nVolunteering is one of the best ways you can give back to your community. Ramsey County has many opportunities to volunteer your time and make a difference.\nAdvisory Boards and Committees\nGet involved with your local government and make a positive impact in your community by serving on an advisory board or committee.\nAdvisory board and committee opportunities\nOutdoors and Recreation\nVolunteers of all ages can help keep parks beautiful and preserve natural resources.\nParks and recreation opportunities\nCorrections and Public Safety\nVolunteers make a real difference in the lives of adults and juvenile offenders.\nCorrections and public safety opportunities\nEmergency response\nHelp Ramsey County provide support and services to residents during an emergency or disaster.\nEmergency response opportunities\nSocial services\nVolunteer as a crisis counselor, or in an office providing clerical support for Social Services or Financial Assistance Services.\nSexual Violence Advocate opportunities\nClerical opportunities\nLibrary\nTeen and adult volunteers can provide a wide variety of different services to help support the Library's mission and goals.\nLibrary opportunities\nVeterans Services\nVolunteers can help local veterans as a court mentor or office assistant.\nVeterans services opportunities\nSkilled opportunities\nRamsey County needs tech-savvy fixers, interpreters, yoga instructors, gardeners, recreation leaders and more.\nSkilled volunteer opportunities\nOpportunities for youth\nA number of volunteer positions with Ramsey County are available for youth ages 12-18.\nOpportunities for youth\nSubscribe to Ramsey County Volunteer News\nCurrent volunteers\nVolunteers should report all of their service hours by using the VicNet Portal.\nVicNet Portal\nVicNet instructions\nBack to top\nConnect with Ramsey County\nA county of excellence working with you to enhance our quality of life.\nContact us Sign up for email updates\nResidents Assistance & Support Elections & Voting Emergency Response & Preparedness Environment Health & Medical Libraries Licenses, Permits & Records Parks & Recreation Property & Home Public Safety & Law Recycling & Waste Roads & Transportation Event Spaces\nBusinesses Doing Business with Ramsey County Workforce & Business Development Licenses, Permits & Inspections Property & Development Recycling & Waste Transit Sales & Use Tax\nYour Government Leadership About Ramsey County Contacts & Locations Departments Projects & Initiatives Ordinances & Regulations Volunteer Open Government\n© 2026 Ramsey County, MN. All rights reserved.\nTerms of Use\nContact Us\nFor Employees\nWeb Accessibility\nPowered by Interpersonal Frequency",
